WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.703
Ideas feel equal until you score them.

00:00:02.703 --> 00:00:03.475
Investors score.

00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:04.633
So do you.

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:08.108
This lesson is about score ideas like an investor.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.652
Urgency, reachability, delivery speed.

00:00:09.652 --> 00:00:12.355
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:12.355 --> 00:00:16.216
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:22.008
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:26.255
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:26.255 --> 00:00:30.888
Stay practical: score three ideas 1–5 before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:35.080
Score urgency, reachability, and delivery speed from one to five.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.791
Remember the objective: score three ideas 1–5.

00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:42.051
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:42.051 --> 00:00:46.698
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:46.698 --> 00:00:50.957
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.957 --> 00:00:55.604
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:58.315
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:58.315 --> 00:00:59.864
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:01:00.184 --> 00:01:02.833
Score three ideas on the same sheet.

00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:05.482
The highest honest total gets fourteen days.

00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:08.132
Remember the objective: score three ideas 1–5.

